(data_only_dirs test)

; [static] profile links a musl-static binary on Alpine; used by the
; Dockerfiles generated by `oi registry docker`. Must be built on
; Alpine 3.22 — 3.23's gcc TLS emits a static-pie binary that segfaults
; at startup (see
; https://discuss.ocaml.org/t/segfaults-on-static-compilation-with-alpine-3-23-fix-no-pie/17800).
;
; [-no-pie] is also required because Alpine's current gcc (14.2+) defaults
; to PIE even on 3.22; without it, ld trips over [crtbeginT.o] at link
; time ("relocation R_X86_64_32 ... can not be used when making a shared
; object"). With [-no-pie] + [-static] we get a classical static ELF that
; runs everywhere.

(env
 (static
  (flags
   (:standard -ccopt -static -ccopt -no-pie))))
